{"version":1,"reference":{"kind":"artifact_content","namespace":"#3663","artifact_type":"_dh-work-item-head-v1","name":"head"},"owner_reference":"#3663","content":"{\"version\":1,\"issue_reference\":\"#3663\",\"parent_revision\":\"923933874a39a42d7b70044692e4f49665b646a6\",\"root_revision\":\"79259522ad9d30e8d3f72c349aa88a8ed58e76dc99af7474bbc1fd0bb21d22d9\",\"body\":\"<!-- backlog-metadata:\\npriority: P2\\ntype: Bug\\nstatus: open\\nadded: 2026-09-20\\n-->\\n\\n## Impact\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nLow-to-moderate: the hint sends the caller to a heavier fallback (`map=True`, itself not budget-bounded \u2014 see #3059) instead of a cheaper, already-supported option (smaller `limit`) when one exists.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Context\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- **Source**: PR #3649 review (codex, thread PRRT_kwDOQGimCs6kFQMK)\\n- **Priority**: P2\\n- **Added**: 2026-09-20\\n- **Research questions**: None\\n</div>\\n\\n## Goal\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nWhen `backlog_view`'s over-budget gate reports `narrowed_to_single_section=True` (caller narrowed to one section via `section=`/`sections=` and it's still over budget), the `_usage` hint tells the caller no smaller retrieval exists and recommends `map=True`. That claim can be false: if the caller also has an active `offset`/`limit` (entry-level pagination within that section) and hasn't reduced `limit` to its minimum, reducing it further is a real, untried narrowing option the hint currently omits.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Reproduction\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n`backlog_view(selector=..., summary=False, section='Log', limit=100)` on a section with many entries, where the `limit=100` page is still over budget. The narrowed `_usage` claims \\\"further section= narrowing is not available for this request\\\" and jumps to `map=True`, without suggesting a smaller `limit`.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Context Prior Discussion\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z-0</sub>\\n\\nSurfaced during PR #3649 (fix/3060-r7-hints, #3060) as the third review round on the same `narrowed_to_single_section` predicate in `plugins/development-harness/backlog_core/server.py`. Two earlier defects in that predicate (raw un-normalized `section=\\\"\\\"`, and a sectionless item's compact-manifest hint) were fixed inline in that PR with regression tests. This one was deferred rather than fixed inline because it's not a boolean-correctness bug like those two \u2014 it's a proposal to broaden the hint's narrowing-space awareness (section state AND entry-pagination state together), which needs `_build_over_budget_view` to receive offset/limit context it doesn't currently take, and a decision on how to state \\\"not fully exhausted\\\" without over-claiming precision.\\n\\nNot a duplicate of #3060: #3060's acceptance criteria cover R7 prohibitions 1-3 for the section-narrowing and map=True mechanisms specifically; this item is about the hint's blindness to a caller's offset/limit pagination state, a distinct narrowing axis #3060 never addressed. Related to the same family of \\\"hint claims more certainty about exhaustion than the code actually knows\\\" as #3059/#3060 criterion 4.\\n\\nUser-provided context: a plausible fix shape is passing the active `offset`/`limit` values into `_build_over_budget_view` and, when `limit != 0`, appending a \\\"try a smaller limit=\\\" suggestion ahead of `map=True` in the narrowed `_usage` text \u2014 but the grooming pass should decide the actual condition for \\\"limit is already minimal enough that further reduction isn't worth suggesting.\\\"\\n</div>\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z-1</sub>\\n\\nSurfaced during PR #3649 (fix/3060-r7-hints, #3060) as the third review round on the same `narrowed_to_single_section` predicate in `plugins/development-harness/backlog_core/server.py`. Two earlier defects in that predicate (raw un-normalized `section=\\\"\\\"`, and a sectionless item's compact-manifest hint) were fixed inline in that PR with regression tests. This one was deferred rather than fixed inline because it's not a boolean-correctness bug like those two \u2014 it's a proposal to broaden the hint's narrowing-space awareness (section state AND entry-pagination state together), which needs `_build_over_budget_view` to receive offset/limit context it doesn't currently take, and a decision on how to state \\\"not fully exhausted\\\" without over-claiming precision.\\n\\nNot a duplicate of #3060: #3060's acceptance criteria cover R7 prohibitions 1-3 for the section-narrowing and map=True mechanisms specifically; this item is about the hint's blindness to a caller's offset/limit pagination state, a distinct narrowing axis #3060 never addressed. Related to the same family of \\\"hint claims more certainty about exhaustion than the code actually knows\\\" as #3059/#3060 criterion 4.\\n\\nUser-provided context: a plausible fix shape is passing the active `offset`/`limit` values into `_build_over_budget_view` and, when `limit != 0`, appending a \\\"try a smaller limit=\\\" suggestion ahead of `map=True` in the narrowed `_usage` text \u2014 but the grooming pass should decide the actual condition for \\\"limit is already minimal enough that further reduction isn't worth suggesting.\\\"\\n</div>\\n\",\"digest\":\"f93572de8eb7f20afd46189c8102d79327f7026a7e52bb598b08e0a606d8c804\",\"comment_id\":\"IC_kwDOQGimCs8AAAABVriN5A\"}"}